camchrome: the web surface Google's variations seed gives every Chrome.

A build that never fetches the seed keeps the field-trial defaults of the source. Diffing every
global and prototype name against Chrome for Testing 158 found 23 names no Chrome 158 has
(document.browsingTopics, window.fence, Fence, FencedFrameConfig, HTMLFencedFrameElement,
attributionSrc on a/area/img/script, XMLHttpRequest.setAttributionReporting, browsingTopics on
img/iframe) and 3 it lacked (navigator.globalPrivacyControl, HTMLAnchorElement.hrefTranslate).
The seed's TopicsDeprecation, AttributionReportingDeprecation and FencedFramesDeprecation studies
switch the first group off and UniversalOptOutSettings turns GlobalPrivacyControlApi on
(testing/variations/fieldtrial_testing_config.json), so the defaults here follow them. The seed disables by override, and
SetRuntimeFeatureFromChromiumFeature() applies a disabled feature only when it is overridden, so
TopicsAPI and AttributionReporting also leave "stable" in runtime_enabled_features.json5, and
GlobalPrivacyControlApi gets an enabled base feature, which is what the runtime state follows.
hrefTranslate exists while the translate service is available; without Google API keys
TranslateManager::IsAvailable() is false and inox turns "offer to translate" off by default, so it
is exposed unless the user turned translation off, as in Chrome.

